@guihong-nv DeepEP requires `num_max_tokens_per_rank` to be identical across all ranks in the communication group. I can synchronize this value when initializing the  buffer. 

However, for THD inputs whose token counts vary across ranks and iterations, recomputing the group-wide maximum each iteration would require a MAX all-reduce followed by `.item()`, introducing an additional GPU-to-CPU synchronization.

  Would it make sense to add an opt-in flag, similar to HybridEP’s `moe_hybridep_pad_uneven_dispatch_inputs`, to support this case? Should we handle this support in a separate PR?

